{"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states","n":"Western American cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["The Western United States has its cuisine, distinct in various ways from that of the rest of the country. States west of Texas, Kansas, Missouri, and Nebraska would be considered part of this area, as would, in some cases, western parts of adjoining states."],["The locavore movement is increasingly influential, as is the concept of sustainability. The influence of the Native American cultures of each area, but especially in the Northwest and in Navajo country, is important in the cuisine picture of the Western United States."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_the_Western_United_States"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"],["Dutch baby pancake","dish/dutch-baby-pancake"],["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Asparagus","ingredient/asparagus"],["Crab meat","ingredient/crab-meat"],["Hard-boiled egg","ingredient/hard-boiled-egg"],["Iceberg lettuce","ingredient/iceberg-lettuce"],["Louis dressing","ingredient/louis-dressing"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Bialy","ingredient/bialy"],["Bialy (bread)","ingredient/bialy-bread"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Sautéed onions","ingredient/sauteed-onions"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Western American cooking","count":4,"links":[["Cuisine of California","cuisine/cuisine-of-california"],["Hawaiian cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-hawaii"],["Pacific Northwest cuisine","cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine"],["Rocky Mountain cuisine","cuisine/rocky-mountain-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas"},"cuisine/maharashtrian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/maharashtrian-cuisine","n":"Maharashtrian cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Maharashtrian or Marathi cuisine is the cuisine of the Marathi people from the Indian state of Maharashtra. It has distinctive attributes, while sharing much with other Indian cuisines. Traditionally, Maharashtrians have considered their food to be more austere than others."],["Maharashtrian cuisine includes mild and spicy dishes. Wheat, rice, jowar, bajri, vegetables, lentils and fruit are dietary staples. Peanuts and cashews are often served with vegetables. Meat was traditionally used sparsely or only by the well-off until recently, because of economic conditions and culture."],["The urban population in metropolitan cities of the state has been influenced by cuisine from other parts of India and abroad. For example, the South Indian dishes idli and dosa, as well as Chinese and Western dishes such as pizza, are popular in home cooking and in restaurants."],["Distinctly Maharashtrian dishes include ukdiche modak, aluchi patal bhaji, kanda pohe and thalipeeth."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"maharashtrian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharashtrian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Shweta in the Kitchen (Maharashtrian)","ref":"site/shwetainthekitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"shwetainthekitchen.com","note":"Maharashtrian section of an Indian home cooking blog.","url":"https://shwetainthekitchen.com/category/maharashtrian/","suggested":true},{"name":"Tarla Dalal (Maharashtrian)","ref":"site/tarladalal-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tarladalal.com","note":"Maharashtrian category on Tarla Dalal's long-running recipe site.","url":"https://www.tarladalal.com/recipes/category/Maharashtrian/?page=3","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Ruchira: Selected Maharashtrian Vegetarian Recipes","ref":"cookbook/ruchira-selected-maharashtrian-vegetarian-recipes","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Kamalabai Ogale","note":"English edition of the best-known Marathi household cookbook.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Pav bhaji","dish/pav-bhaji"],["Usal","dish/usal"],["Vada pav","dish/vada-pav"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Bread roll","ingredient/bread-roll"],["Lentil","ingredient/lentil"],["Batata vada","ingredient/batata-vada"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Maharashtrian cooking","count":1,"links":[["Hridhaansh cuisine","cuisine/hridhaansh-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"cuisine/samoan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/samoan-cuisine","n":"Samoan cuisine","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Oceania","cuisines#oceania"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Samoa","intro":[["The traditional culture of Samoa is a communal way of life based on Fa'a Samoa, the unique socio-political culture. In Samoan culture, most activities are done together. The traditional living quarters, or fale (houses), contain no walls and up to 20 people may sleep on the ground in the same fale. During the day, the fale is used for chatting and relaxing. One's family is viewed as an integral part of a person's life. The aiga or extended family lives and works together. Elders in the family are greatly respected and hold the highest status, and this may be seen at a traditional Sunday umu (normal oven)."],["Samoan culture is present in both the Independent State of Samoa and in American Samoa (a territory of the United States)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"samoan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samoan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Polynesian Cultural Center Blog: Samoan recipes","ref":"site/blog-polynesia-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"blog.polynesia.com","note":"Samoan dishes such as palusami from the Hawaii cultural center's blog, written with its Pacific Islander staff.","url":"https://blog.polynesia.com/tag/samoan-recipe","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Mea'ai Samoa: Recipes and Stories from the Heart of Polynesia","ref":"cookbook/mea-ai-samoa-recipes-and-stories-from-the-heart-of-polynesia","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Robert Oliver, Tracy Berno and Shiri Ram, 2013","note":"Samoa-focused follow-up to Me'a Kai, tracing dishes back to local growers; won a Gourmand award.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781775534273","suggested":true},{"name":"Me'a Kai: The Food and Flavours of the South Pacific","ref":"cookbook/me-a-kai-the-food-and-flavours-of-the-south-pacific","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Robert Oliver, Tracy Berno and Shiri Ram, 2010","note":"Regional cookbook with a chapter of Samoan recipes from island cooks.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28452199M","suggested":true}]}],"cont":"Oceanic cuisine"},"dish/auguste-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/auguste-restaurant","n":"Auguste (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Restaurant Auguste is a restaurant in Maarssen, Netherlands. It is a fine dining restaurant that was awarded one Michelin star in 2006 and retained that rating until 